# Releases

[`Version.xcconfig`](Version.xcconfig) is the only shipping version. The runbook is [`RELEASE.md`](RELEASE.md). Commands live in [`scripts/release.py`](scripts/release.py).

## Channels

- **Dev** is a Debug run. Bundle id `com.collinbrowse.thesilverscreen.dev`, display name Silver Dev. It does not advance the build number.
- **TestFlight** is an archive of the commit tagged `testflight/<marketing>+<build>`.
- **App Store** is that same commit, tagged `v<marketing>`. Promote it. Do not archive a second binary for the store.

## Rules

- Change versions with `python3 scripts/release.py`. Leave `MARKETING_VERSION` and `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION` out of the app target in `project.pbxproj` — those lines override the xcconfig. Test targets keep their own numbers.
- A feature commit does not bump the version. `bump` is for the next marketing version. `cut` is the only thing that advances the build.
- `cut` and `promote` commit or tag from a clean tree. Do not hand-tag, and do not retarget `v*` without `promote --retarget`.
- Upload uses an App Store Connect API key from the environment. Never commit a `.p8` file.
- No Fastlane and no other third-party release tool. Archive with `scripts/release.py archive`.
- Debug is Silver Dev / `.dev`. Release (TestFlight and App Store) is Silver Screen / shipping bundle id. Never put Dev branding on Release. `python3 scripts/release.py check` and `archive` enforce this.
